WEBVTT

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:52.690
So, come on in.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.760
Ma'am Benna? Somewhere in the jungle of Baladora?

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.400
Cool!

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.550
I'd like you to meet Mark, my son.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:07.420
Well thank you very much. The first guy I've met in the last year and a half who isn't a jerk and now he thinks I've got a crazy kid.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:14.630
I'm not crazy, Mom. This thing was a lie. I saw it. Why won't you believe me?

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:20.610
Honey, what I believe is that you fell asleep with this thing in your hand and you dreamt the whole thing.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:26.360
It didn't seem like a dream.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.000
You know, I'm surprised you don't have nightmares in here all the time.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.220
Look at this place.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:40.850
I didn't argue when you wanted a palm tree or a leopard skin rug, but a red ant farm?

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:45.490
Things are... they're getting out of hand, Mark.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.810
Mark, are you listening to me?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.120
- You killed me.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.910
- Don't tempt me.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.830
And what's this Kalia?

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.470
It's not some foreign swear word, is it?

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.910
- No, no, it's a word I made up.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.450
It sort of makes me feel stronger.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.670
- Well, how convenient.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.210
And since you're feeling so strong,

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:20.940
maybe you won't mind Kalia-ing up this place.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:22.290
All of it.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:23.130
- What?

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:23.970
- You heard me.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.270
I want all this jungle stuff out of here.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:30.000
No more shrunken heads, no more masks, no tom-toms.

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:34.920
I don't even want to see a coconut in here unless it's sliced up in a fruit salad.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.890
Is that clear?

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:38.900
Is it?

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.680
Yeah, Mom.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:42.680
Now go to bed.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:52.820
Thanks a lot.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.000
Thank you very much.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:36.690
Hello? Hello? Benna? I can hardly hear you!

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:41.560
How's it going down there? Met any nice crocodiles lately?

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:43.280
I want to talk to her.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:47.280
Yes, yeah, he got it yesterday. Honestly, Benna, a shrunken head.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.290
Couldn't you have sent him a nice sweater or something?

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:56.080
Oh, all right, hang on. Keep it short, it's long distance.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.920
Aunt Benna! Hi! Yeah, it's great, thanks.

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:03.620
- I just had the strangest dream about you.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:07.080
- Uh-huh, yeah.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:07.900
- What?

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:08.900
- No way!

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:15.550
- Mom wants me to come and visit her on the island about--

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:17.780
- Benno, what's going on?

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:19.240
- Well, yeah, of course he'd love it.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:23.920
I just don't think, two weeks?

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.620
You want me to send my son away from home

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.360
to a jungle on the other side of the world

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:29.760
for two whole weeks?

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:33.910
When?

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:01.510
27.

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:22.410
Sorry.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.260
Aliyah.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.750
Aliyah.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:27.040
How'd you know that?

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.200
How you doing? I'm Jimmy.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.320
I'm your pilot.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.590
Why do I need a pilot?

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:49.400
Camp's a whole day away by road.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.690
And it's too dangerous to drive anyway.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:52.980
So your plane's safer?

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.980
Uh, no.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:56.210
But it's faster!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:28.870
America right? You live in Hollywood? You live near Hollywood?

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:41.330
you ever been to hollywood no oh i'm going to hollywood really uh-huh gonna be a movie star

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:49.240
listen oh fine cool huh yeah great

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.160
Okay, big engine trouble!

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:04.660
I told you there was nothing to worry about.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:21.980
Some supplies here for the camp.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:25.810
Food, some medicine, and this.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.470
Very important.

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:28.320
What is it?

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:29.520
Licorice gum.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.520
- Dr. Hollings loves his licorice gunk.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:33.680
- Who's Dr. Hollings?

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:36.550
- My father, the mad scientist.

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:38.730
- Hey, Corrine, this is Mark, Benna's--

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:39.400
- Nephew.

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:40.420
- I know.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:41.860
Well, welcome to the jungle.

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:42.780
- Thanks.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:43.890
Where's Aunt Benna?

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:45.820
- Did you remember my CDs?

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:46.660
- The latest.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:47.760
- Yes, Jimmy, thanks.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:48.920
You're a lifesaver.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:51.700
- Miss Hollings ain't a big fan of jungle living.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:52.590
- Really?

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:54.570
How would you like to spend a year of your life

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:56.990
in the world's biggest salad?

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:59.320
Come on, see you next week, Jimmy.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.340
- Thanks for the ride, Jimmy.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:09.710
- Be careful, Mark.

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:16.680
- Have fun!

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:36.790
place is so cool oh yeah fun city well it's better than my neighborhood I mean

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:41.460
a bunch of boring houses full of boring people wouldn't you rather live here let

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:47.170
me draw you a map if I even have to look at another fried banana I will throw

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:58.610
myself into the tiger pit this way they have tigers here

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:03.650
He's here.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:13.670
Mark, handsome as your picture.

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:15.290
Isn't he handsome, Corrine?

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.610
He's kind of short.

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:18.810
Oh, don't pay any attention to her, Mark.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.310
She's just an old grumpy Gus sometimes.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:22.810
I'm Dr. Hallings.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:24.450
Well, one of them anyway.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.350
You just call me Carolyn.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:30.000
So, what do you think of our luxury vacation resort so far?

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.220
I love it. Where's Aunt Benna?

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:40.260
Let me give you the two-quid tour. This is the lab. This is where we've been doing our research.

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:44.260
Wait a sec. This is all really fascinating and everything, but I kind of want to see my aunt.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:46.260
Is she in her tent or something?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.260
Not exactly.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:54.380
Mark, this is my husband, Richard. The other Dr. Hallings.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:59.070
What do you mean, not exactly? Where is she?

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:00.000
I'm...

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:18.410
afraid we don't know she's disappeared we didn't want to worry you unnecessarily

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:22.210
she's my favorite aunt in the world i think i'm allowed to be just a little worried look

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:26.560
benna is always wandering off on her own taking these solo adventures

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:30.000
yesterday she went out in the morning and just never came back i'm sure it's nothing

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:31.970
serious. But we're organizing

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.650
a search party just to be unsafe, sir.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:35.600
Good. When do we leave? No, no, no, no.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.430
Not we. You stay put.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.620
This jungle is far too dangerous

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:41.040
for someone who doesn't know their way around.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:43.190
Yeah, well, you obviously haven't seen my bedroom.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:47.930
Don't move. What? Is there something on me?

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:49.050
A bug?

00:14:51.970 --> 00:15:00.000
Licorice gum. What are you doing, you clumsy fool?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.380
That's valuable equipment!

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.350
It's gonna be alright, Mark.

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:07.780
My father might seem a little strange,

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:10.240
but he knows the jungle inside out.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.930
Something's happened to her.

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:15.470
What if she's...

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:16.290
We'll find her.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:33.640
Ampanna?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.480
- Just a dream.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:04.860
- Dream.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:24.670
- Dream.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:25.890
- You want me to follow you?

00:17:48.780 --> 00:18:00.000
Hello, this is Dr. Benna Thomas, and I've just been joined on this project by Drs. Richard

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:10.030
from Miskatonic University. And we will be continuing my research into this room. They

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:17.470
make a very strong T. Bella, I was just going through your old nose and I found this reference

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:28.100
to something called Keha Lahia. It was in a trunk in your tent. I was looking for a map

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.000
and I... This is private, Carolyn. I really would appreciate

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.310
if you would just stay out of my tent, please?

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:33.440
We're...

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:34.320
And I am...

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:34.700
Matan!

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:35.280
Matan!

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:15.150
Hollings 2.0, Hollings 2.0. Come in, point zero. I repeat, Hollings 2.0. Come in, point zero.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:20.070
Point zero, I repeat, this is point zero. What is your status? Over.

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:29.150
I'm afraid there's still no sign of our Dr. Thomas. She knows this jungle very well. She can survive out there indefinitely.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:40.270
problem. There may be a solution. We have her nephew. Hostage. We prefer to think of him as

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:46.310
our special guest. I suspect he may be the one thing that can help us get through to the good

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:53.270
doctor. My pleasure. Over and out.

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:14.640
quite sure, but Dr. Hollings is up to something.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:16.260
He might be lying about my aunt.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.750
Is there a phone or something around here that I can use? I have to

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.580
call the police. Hey.

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:23.190
Hey, are you listening to me? Hey!

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:23.910
Hey!

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:36.730
I'm sorry, Mark. I'm afraid he can't move.

00:20:36.730 --> 00:20:39.860
In fact, I'm afraid you're not going anywhere.
